  classification - What type /category
    - Learn from the labeled data to categorize new inputs into predefined classes
    Types:
      - Binary classification (yes or no / 1 or 0 / true or false)
        Common Algorithms
          Logistic Regression
          Support Vector Machine (SVM)
          Decision Tree
          Random Forest
          K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)
          Naïve Bayes
      - Multi - class classification
        - one class from three or more possible classes.
        -  Each observation belongs to exactly one class
        Common Algorithms  
          Decision Tree
          Random Forest
          Support Vector Machine (One-vs-Rest)
          K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)
          Neural Networks

      - Multi - label classification
       - multiple classes at the same time. 
       - Unlike multiclass classification, an instance can have more than one label.
       Common Algorithms
          Binary Relevance
          Classifier Chains
          Random Forest
          Neural Networks
        
      - Imbalanced Classification
        - significantly more samples than the other classes.
         Common Solutions
          Oversampling (SMOTE)
          Undersampling
          Class Weighting
          Ensemble Methods

